  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set version = \"0.10.0\" %}\n{% set fork_version = \"1.0.1\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: ojph\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/o/ojph/ojph-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: bab1ca6175f904e012410ab49bda98b213a5701c1bcfd8212f4b50274441ef72\n  # Since 0.10.0, ojph statically links the \"ojph\" fork of OpenJPH (renamed\n  # so it is co-installable with upstream OpenJPH) instead of linking the\n  # openjph package. The static link is deliberate: this Python package is\n  # the fork's only consumer and the two are co-developed and released\n  # together, so there is no library to share with other packages. The tag\n  # ojph-{{ fork_version }} pins git hash\n  # f03eff4909aa3f0538949e0a2ef3d20f23a39994.\n  - url: https://github.com/hmaarrfk/OpenJPH/archive/refs/tags/ojph-{{ fork_version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: a7a22ed59e5b863883e675ae92dc7a9b01e2a8cd0b40c746f6f6776ee0e84293\n    folder: subprojects/ojph\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: true  # [py<312]\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - {{ compiler('c') }}\n    - {{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools\n    - pybind11\n    # header-only build dependency of the vendored fork (Google Highway\n    # SIMD kernels); nothing is linked at run time\n    - libhwy\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy >=2.1\n\ntest:\n  requires:\n    - pip\n  commands:\n    - pip check\n  imports:\n    - ojph\n\nabout:\n  home: https://github.com/ramonaoptics/ojph\n  summary: 'Python bindings for OpenJPH, a JPEG 2000 codec'\n  license: BSD-3-Clause AND BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE.txt\n    - subprojects/ojph/LICENSE\n  dev_url: https://github.com/ramonaoptics/ojph\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - hmaarrfk\n",
